      "Google Trends — check breakout/rising related queries specifically, not just top queries (breakout = velocity signal, top queries are usually already saturated)",
      "Google search — '[current month] [year] nail trends' and 'nails trending now' — read what's already being covered, to distinguish a genuinely early angle from an already-saturated one",
      "site:quora.com nail trends [current season/month] — real audience curiosity signal",
      "Best-effort per research_source_rules: site:pinterest.com [current month/season] nails, YouTube search for recent upload velocity on nail terms — try once each, use if usable, move on if not"
